course: dictionary
lesson: 10635
title: Unhealthy and its meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unhealthy means not good for your health. «Some countries limit adverts for unhealthy food aimed at children.» The word food tells you what kind of thing is unhealthy: food that can harm your body if you eat too much of it, like sweets, crisps and fizzy drinks.
explain: Unhealthy can also describe a living thing that is not well. A plant with yellow leaves may be unhealthy, because it is not growing properly. Here the clue is the plant, so unhealthy means not well, or looking ill.
explain: Unhealthy can also mean not good or normal, as in an unhealthy friendship. To choose the right meaning, ask what the word describes. Is it food, a living thing, or something like a friendship? The clues around the word will tell you which meaning fits.
fact: Unhealthy is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like food, plant or habit.
fact: Comparing forms: unhealthy, unhealthier, unhealthiest, or more unhealthy and most unhealthy.
fact: «Unhealthy» means not good for your health, or not well, or not good or normal.
fact: Common phrases are unhealthy food, unhealthy snacks and unhealthy habits.
fact: The opposite of unhealthy in the first meaning is healthy: a healthy snack is good for your body.
exercise: «Some countries limit adverts for unhealthy food aimed at children.» What does unhealthy mean here? | *Not good for your health | Very cold to touch | Full of healthy vitamins | Made by children
exercise: Ella says, «The plant on the windowsill has yellow leaves and looks unhealthy.» What does unhealthy mean here? | *Not well, or looking ill | Giving out light | Very tall and green | Made of plastic
exercise: Which is the correct comparative form of unhealthy? | unhealthiness | *unhealthier | unhealthyer | more unhealthiest
test: In a health lesson, which of these would be called an unhealthy food? | Apple | Carrot | *Fizzy drink | Glass of water
test: What does «unhealthy habits» most likely mean? | Habits you do only in the morning | *Habits that are not good for your health | Habits of birds | Habits that are good for your body
exam: Which sentence uses unhealthy to mean not well, or looking ill? | Grandma wore an unhealthy hat | *The fern had brown, drooping leaves and looked unhealthy | I ate an unhealthy apple for lunch | The unhealthy boy won the race
